on More Actions Previous Job Job Title Technical Services Librarian Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 2959237 Business Unit Valley City State University Location Valley City Posted 05/28/2026 Full/Part Time Full-Time Department Library Close Date Open Until Filled Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Position Information Job Title Full-Time, 12-Month, Benefited Position Number: 00009568 Internal/External Position Description Allen Memorial Library at Valley City State University (VCSU) seeks a full-time Technical Services Librarian responsible for technical services, expanding access, improving discovery, and aligning the library with emerging best practices. This position also contributes to broader library services including reference assistance and promotion of library collections. Responsibilities •    Perform cataloging of all library resources efficiently and accurately using professional standards and best practices. •    Manage the physical processing of library materials. •    Play a key role in managing the library’s digital and special collections. •    Develop procedures, training, and instructional documentation for technical services and library systems. •    Support the administration and maintenance of resource platforms, discovery tools, and related applications in collaboration with consortia partners and campus technology staff. •    Troubleshoot access to online resources and provide solution articles for the library's knowledge base. •    Assist with gathering and reporting library statistics and assessment. •    Assist with promoting library collections and services as valuable resources for the VCSU community and beyond. •    Engage with emerging practices in cataloging, metadata, electronic resources, accessibility, and library systems. •    Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications •    Master's degree in Library Information Science from an ALA-accredited program. Preferred Qualifications •    Knowledge of cataloging and metadata standards, including MARC, RDA, authority control, and classification practices. •    Demonstrated ability to manage detailed work accurately, analyze problems, and improve workflows. •    Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in a team oriented academic environment. •    Experience with integrated library systems. •    Experience with developing or managing digital collections, institutional repositories, or archives. •    Experience with digital accessibility. Compensation $58,000 - 62,000 depending on experience and qualifications. Benefits VCSU offers a competitive and comprehensive benefits package which includes health insurance plans with premiums fully paid for by the university, TIAA/NDPERS retirement plan, life insurance, annual and sick leave, paid holidays, Employee Assistance Program, tuition waivers, and wellness incentives. Additional benefits available include supplemental life, dental, vision, flexible spending account, and supplemental retirement plans. Click here for more information . Application Information Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. A criminal background check will be conducted on all hires. Submit your application materials online including cover letter, resume, and contact information for references. Preference given to applications received on or before June 11, and review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Additional Information For more information, or for accommodations contact: human.resources@vcsu.edu . For North Dakota Relay Services, go to: https://www.relaynorthdakota.com/ . This position is subject to the North Dakota Veteran's Preference procedure. Proof of eligibility can include a DD-214, a copy of NGB 22 from National Guard or Reserve (with a unit located in ND) or certification from the applicant's unit command that the individual is expected to be discharged or released from active duty in the uniformed services under other than dishonorable conditions not lat