tion More Actions Previous Job Job Title VCSU Student Employee Football - Filmer Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 2959542 Business Unit Valley City State University Location Valley City Posted 07/23/2026 Full/Part Time Part-Time Department Athletics - Football Close Date Open Until Filled Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Position Information This is a part-time, non-benefited position. Only VCSU students are eligible to be hired in this position. Unsolicited applications to this posting will NOT be considered or responded to. This position is subjected to North Dakota Veteran's Preference requirements. A criminal background check will be conducted on all hires. Submit your application materials online including cover letter, resume, and contact information for references. Preference given to applications received on or before July 27, 2025, and a review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Title: VCSU Student Employee Football - Filmer Department: Athletics - Football Reports to: Raynor Beierle - Assistant Football Coach Position Summary: As a student filmer for the department of Athletics-Football, your primary role is to film football activities including games and practices throughout the week. The ideal candidate will be able to work 10-20 hours every week, mostly evenings and weekends during home games. The candidate should have some background knowledge of filming football events. The amount of hours will vary based on how many home events are held each week. Responsibilities/Expectations: Maintain confidentiality. Performs other duties as required or assigned pertinent to the position. Must be a positive role model on and off the job. Must know and abide by all University rules and regulations. Must maintain a positive attitude toward the position. Qualifications/Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Be a full-time undergraduate student (basic). Minimum of 10 hours per week Self-motivated and ability to work unsupervised. TRAINING WILL BE PROVIDED Skill in observing situations. Ability to work and make decisions with minimal supervision. Good interpersonal skills and desire to be a team player. Good organization skills. Effectively be able to operate a video camera. Physical Demands Regularly required to move about. Be able to effectively carry equipment. Contact Information: Please refer position questions to raynor.beierle@vcsu.edu or call 509-346-8714. If you would like assistance with your application, please contact Janna Kohler, Director for Career Services at janna.kohler@vcsu.edu or 701.845.7534. Apply for Job Explore Jobs Sign In New User"
