tion More Actions Previous Job Job Title VCSU Student Employee for Athletics Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 2959683 Business Unit Valley City State University Location Valley City Posted 08/10/2026 Full/Part Time Part-Time Department Athletics - Administration Close Date Open Until Filled Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Position Information This is a part-time, non-benefited position. Only VCSU students are eligible to be hired in this position. This position is subjected to North Dakota Veteran's Preference requirements. Title : VCSU Student Employee for Athletics Department : Athletics Reports to : Steve Olson Position Summary: As a student assistant in the department of Athletics, your primary role is to support the VCSU game day activities and the athletic department. The ideal candidate will be able to work 5-10 hours every other week, mostly nights and weekends during home games, and should have some working knowledge of athletics. However, we are willing to train the right candidates. The amount of hours will vary based on how many home events are held each week. Students may be asked to run scoreboard, game clock, shot clock, stat call, fill out the scorebook, run video camera, oversight of video replay, or other similar duties on game day. Students will also have opportunities to work Barnes County basketball tournaments along with District/Regional tournament games. Contact Information: Please refer position questions to Steve Olson at steven.c.olson@vcsu.edu or call 701-845-7162. If you would like assistance with your application, please contact Career Services at janna.kohler@vcsu.edu. If interested, click on the Apply for Job button. Resume and Cover Letter not required, but a cover letter is recommended to explain your knowledge of athletics. Apply for Job Explore Jobs Sign In New User"
    },
