tion More Actions Previous Job Job Title VCSU Student Lab Tech - Science Department Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 2959780 Business Unit Valley City State University Location Valley City Posted 08/20/2026 Full/Part Time Part-Time Department Science Close Date Open Until Filled Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Position Information This is a part-time, non-benefited position. Only VCSU students are eligible to be hired in this position. Unsolicited applications to this posting will NOT be considered or responded to. This position is subjected to North Dakota Veteran's Preference requirements. Title: VCSU Student Lab Tech Department: Science Department Reports to: Dr. Bob Anderson Position Summary: The Science Department is looking for a student to help with specimen preservation and with the vertebrate collections.  Preference will be given to a student with freeze dryer and vertebrate collections experience. 3-4 Hours / M-F. No Weekends. Responsibilities/Expectations: Maintain confidentiality. Performs other duties as required or assigned pertinent to the position. Must be a positive role model on and off the job. Must know and abide by all University rules and regulations. Must maintain a positive attitude toward the position. Qualifications/Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Be a full-time undergraduate student (basic). Self-motivated and ability to work unsupervised. TRAINING WILL BE PROVIDED Skill in observing situations. Ability to work and make decisions with minimal supervision. Good interpersonal skills and desire to be a team player. Experience with customer service- common courtesy in working with students, employees, and the public. Good organization and time management skills. Physical Demands Regularly required to move about and lift items Contact Information: Please refer position questions to bob.anderson@vcsu.edu If you would like assistance with your application, please contact Janna Kohler, Director for Career Services at janna.kohler@vcsu.edu or 701.845.7534. Apply for Job Explore Jobs Sign In New User"
