tion More Actions Previous Job Job Title VCSU Student Intramural Referee Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 2959842 Business Unit Valley City State University Location Valley City Posted 08/28/2026 Full/Part Time Part-Time Department Housing Close Date Open Until Filled Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Position Information This is a part-time, non-benefited position. Only VCSU students are eligible to be hired in this position. Unsolicited applications to this posting will NOT be considered or responded to. This position is subjected to North Dakota Veteran's Preference requirements. Title: VCSU Student Intramural Referee Department: Intramurals / Student Affairs Reports to: Joe Wright, Intramural Coordinator Position Summary : The VCSU Intramural Flag Football Referee is responsible for officiating intramural flag football games while helping create a safe, fair, competitive, and enjoyable experience for all participants. Referees will enforce league rules, identify and call fouls, keep track of scores and game clock, and assist with the overall operation of intramural events. This position is an excellent opportunity for students who enjoy sports, working with others, and creating a positive campus community. Pay starts at $10 an hour. Responsibilities : Officiate VCSU intramural flag football games. Enforce VCSU intramural rules and flag football regulations. Identify and call fouls, penalties, and violations. Keep track of the score, downs, game clock, and possession. Communicate rules and decisions clearly and respectfully to participants. Maintain control of games and help resolve conflicts when they arise. Promote good sportsmanship and respectful behavior. Help create a welcoming and inclusive environment for all participants. Arrive on time and prepared for assigned games. Assist with field setup, equpment, and game operations when needed. Report injuries, major incidents, or sportsmanship concerns to the Intramural Coordinator. Help answer participant questions and provide information about intramural programs. Represent VCSU Campus Recreation in a professional and positive manner. Attend required referee training prior to the beginning of the season. Qualifications : Must be a currently enrolled VCSU student. Previous football, flag football, officiating, or sports experience is preferred but not required . Ability to make fair and confident decisions. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to remain calm and professional during disagreements. Dependable and punctual. Comfortable working with students from a variety of backgrounds and experience levels. Willingness to learn and apply intramural rules. Physical Demands : Regularly required to move about.  Will be running or walking most of your games. Contact Information : Please refer position questions to joseph.d.wright@vcsu.edu or call 701-845-7932. If you would like assistance with your application, please contact Janna Kohler, Director for Career Services at janna.kohler@vcsu.edu or 701.845.7534. Apply for Job Explore Jobs Sign In New User"
    },
